<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000064> a skos:Concept;
  dc:identifier "homoit0000064";
  dc:issued "2019-05-14"^^xsd:date;
  dc:modified "2025-02-23"^^xsd:date;
  dc:replaces <http://homosaurus.org/v2/aphallia>;
  rdfs:comment "People with aphallia have XY chromosomes, testes, and are born without a penis. They produce typical levels of testosterone, and they develop secondary sex characteristics associated with a typical testosterone puberty during adolescence.",
    "Las personas con afalia tienen cromosomas XY, testículos y nacen sin pene. Producen niveles típicos de testosterona y desarrollan características sexuales secundarias asociadas a una pubertad típica con testosterona durante la adolescencia.";
  skos:altLabel "Penile agenesis";
  skos:broader <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000669>;
  skos:changeNote "Version 4.1.0";
  skos:hasTopConcept <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001269>;
  skos:inScheme <https://homosaurus.org/v3>;
  skos:prefLabel "Aphallia",
    "Afalia" .

<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000072> a skos:Concept;
  dc:identifier "homoit0000072";
  dc:issued "2019-05-14"^^xsd:date;
  dc:modified "2025-02-23"^^xsd:date;
  dc:replaces <http://homosaurus.org/v2/ashtime>;
  rdfs:comment "Term used by the Maale people in Ethiopia for people assigned male at birth who exhibit feminine characteristics; there is some question over the legitimacy of term.",
    "Término utilizado por el pueblo Maale de Etiopía para las personas asignadas al sexo masculino al nacer que presentan características femeninas; hay cuestionamientos sobre la legitimidad del término.";
  skos:broader <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000322>;
  skos:changeNote "Version 4.1.0";
  skos:hasTopConcept <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560>;
  skos:inScheme <https://homosaurus.org/v3>;
  skos:prefLabel "Ashtime" .

<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000084> a skos:Concept;
  dc:identifier "homoit0000084";
  dc:issued "2019-05-14"^^xsd:date;
  dc:modified "2025-02-23"^^xsd:date;
  dc:replaces <http://homosaurus.org/v2/aversionTherapy>;
  rdfs:comment "Behavior modification therapy intended to displace pleasant associations evoked by homosexuality with unpleasant ones (in the form of electric shocks or nausea-inducing drugs) in order to shift the subject's homosexual orientation to a heterosexual one.",
    "Terapia de modificación de comportamiento que busca sustituir asociaciones placenteras evocadas por la homosexualidad con otras desagradables (utilizando descargas eléctricas o fármacos que provocan náuseas) con el fin de cambiar la orientación homosexual del sujeto por una heterosexual.";
  skos:broader <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000106>;
  skos:changeNote "Version 4.1.0";
  skos:exactMatch <http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85010520>;
  skos:hasTopConcept <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001004>;
  skos:inScheme <https://homosaurus.org/v3>;
  skos:prefLabel "Aversion therapy",
    "Terapia de aversión";
  skos:related <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000303> .

<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000085> a skos:Concept;
  dc:identifier "homoit0000085";
  dc:issued "2019-05-14"^^xsd:date;
  dc:modified "2025-04-23"^^xsd:date;
  dc:replaces <http://homosaurus.org/v2/aylonit>;
  rdfs:comment "A romanized version of the Hebrew term traditionally used in Judaism to describe people assigned female at birth who develop secondary-sex characteristics perceived as \"male\" as well as fertility issues.",
    "Término hebreo que se refiere a una mujer con desarrollo masculino que suele ser infértil.";
  skos:broader <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000322>;
