  dc:replaces <http://homosaurus.org/v2/tidaWena>;
  rdfs:comment "In Venezuela's indigenous Warao culture, this term refers to people assigned male at birth who are thought to possess two spirits and often assume a spiritual role; translates to \"twisted women.\"",
    "En la cultura indígena warao de Venezuela, este término se refiere a las personas asignadas al sexo masculino al nacer y que se cree que poseen dos espíritus y que, a menudo, asumen un papel espiritual; se traduce como \"mujeres retorcidas\".";
  skos:broader <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000322>;
  skos:changeNote "Version 4.1.0";
  skos:hasTopConcept <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560>;
  skos:inScheme <https://homosaurus.org/v3>;
