<https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000898> a skos:Concept;
  dc:identifier "homoit0000898";
  dc:issued "2019-05-14"^^xsd:date;
  dc:modified "2025-02-23"^^xsd:date;
  dc:replaces <http://homosaurus.org/v2/takatapui>;
  rdfs:comment "Term used by the Māori people, or people who are part of the Indigenous Polynesian people of mainland Aotearoa (New Zealand), that was historically used to describe an \"intimate companion of the same sex.\" In the 1980s, the term was reclaimed for use by lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender, queer, intersex people, and other members of Rainbow communities. Only use to refer to individuals who identify as Takatāpui.",
    "Término utilizado por el pueblo maorí, o personas que forman parte del pueblo indígena polinesio de la parte continental de Aotearoa (Nueva Zelanda), que históricamente se utilizó para describir a un \"compañero íntimo del mismo sexo\". En la década de 1980, el término fue reclamado para ser utilizado por personas lesbianas, gay, bisexuales, transgénero, queer, intersex y otros miembros de las comunidades arcoíris. Utilícese únicamente para referirse a personas que se identifiquen como takatāpui.";
  skos:altLabel "LGBTQ+ Māori people",
    "Māori (LGBTQ)",
    "Māori LGBTQ+ people",
    "Personas LGBTQ+ Maori",
    "Personas LGBTQ+ Māori";
  skos:broader <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000322>,
    <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000886>,
    <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001297>;
  skos:changeNote "Version 4.1.0";
  skos:hasTopConcept <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0000560>;
  skos:inScheme <https://homosaurus.org/v3>;
  skos:prefLabel "Takatāpui";
  skos:related <https://homosaurus.org/v4/homoit0001810> .

