  dc:replaces <http://homosaurus.org/v2/goddessMovementLesbian>;
  rdfs:comment "A spiritual movement that emerged in North America, Western Europe, Australia, and New Zealand in 1970s in response to male-dominated organized religion; involves worshiping the Goddess (or several goddesses), as well as a focus on women, femininity, and feminism; often associated with lesbian communities.",
    "Un movimiento espiritual que surgió en Norteamérica, Europa Occidental, Australia y Nueva Zelanda en la década de 1970 en respuesta a la religión organizada dominada por los hombres; implica adorar a la Diosa (o varias diosas), así como la centralidad de las mujeres, la feminidad y el feminismo; a menudo asociado con comunidades lésbicas.";
  skos:altLabel "Goddess movement (Lesbians)",
    "Goddess religion";
  skos:changeNote "Version 4.1.0";
  skos:closeMatch <http://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh89003267>;
